From: Airtype downstream
Subject: [PATCH] common : return no speculative types for a GGUF without a u32 block count

common_speculative_types_from_gguf passes the result of
gguf_find_key(ctx, "<arch>.block_count") straight to gguf_get_val_u32. When the key is missing
the id is -1, and gguf_get_val_u32 aborts the process on GGML_ASSERT(key_id >= 0 && ...); a
key of another type aborts on the type assertion instead. The function already returns an empty
list for a file it cannot read or whose general.architecture is missing, so a file without a
usable block count now gets the same answer instead of taking the process down.

Such files exist wherever GGUFs are handled by path: a multimodal projector (general.architecture
"clip", whose block counts live under clip.vision.* and clip.audio.*), a LoRA adapter, or a
truncated download. Every model llama.cpp can load stores <arch>.block_count as a u32, so the
result for loadable models is unchanged.

Upstream: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/28099 makes the same change for the
missing key and is still open and unmerged; the unguarded lookup is on master as of 95887577
(2026-09-26). This patch also guards the key's type. Drop it once a fix is in the pinned release.

Validated against llama.cpp b11201 through llama_rs_model_file_has_mtp_layers, which calls this
function directly: the airtype-desktop-inference-sidecar-engine test
a_gguf_without_a_block_count_has_no_mtp_layers reports false for a GGUF holding only
general.architecture = "clip" and for one whose block count is a string, where the unpatched
function aborts, and the engine's speculative-decoding suite still detects the NextN layers of
Qwen3.5-4B-MTP and decodes speculatively with them.

--- a/common/speculative.cpp
+++ b/common/speculative.cpp
@@ -2303,7 +2303,12 @@
 
     const std::string arch = gguf_get_val_str(gguf_ctx.get(), arch_id);
     if (arch != "dflash") {
-        const uint32_t block_count = gguf_get_val_u32(gguf_ctx.get(), gguf_find_key(gguf_ctx.get(), (arch + ".block_count").c_str()));
+        const int64_t block_count_id = gguf_find_key(gguf_ctx.get(), (arch + ".block_count").c_str());
+        if (block_count_id < 0 || gguf_get_kv_type(gguf_ctx.get(), block_count_id) != GGUF_TYPE_UINT32) {
+            return {};
+        }
+
+        const uint32_t block_count = gguf_get_val_u32(gguf_ctx.get(), block_count_id);
 
         if (gguf_find_tensor(gguf_ctx.get(), ("blk." + std::to_string(block_count - 1) + ".nextn.eh_proj.weight").c_str()) >= 0) {
             return { COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_DRAFT_MTP };
